#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:128
msgid "Path-like syntax"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:130
msgid ""
"Flakes corresponding to a local path can also be referred to by a direct "
"path reference, either `/absolute/path/to/the/flake` or`./relative/path/to/"
"the/flake`. Note that the leading `./` is mandatory for relative paths. If "
"it is omitted, the path will be interpreted as [URL-like syntax](#url-like-"
"syntax), which will cause error messages like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:140
msgid "The semantic of such a path is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:142
msgid ""
"If the directory is part of a Git repository, then the input will be treated "
"as a `git+file:` URL, otherwise it will be treated as a `path:` url;"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:143
msgid ""
"If the directory doesn't contain a `flake.nix` file, then Nix will search "
"for such a file upwards in the file system hierarchy until it finds any of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:144
msgid "The Git repository root, or"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:145
msgid "The filesystem root (/), or"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:146
msgid "A folder on a different mount point."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:148
msgid ""
"Contrary to URL-like references, path-like flake references can contain "
"arbitrary unicode characters (except `#` and `?`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:152
msgid "`.`: The flake to which the current directory belongs."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:153
msgid "`/home/alice/src/patchelf`: A flake in some other directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:154
msgid ""
"`./../sub directory/with Ûñî©ôδ€`: A flake in another relative directory "
"that has Unicode characters in its name."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:157
msgid "Flake reference attributes"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:159
msgid "The following generic flake reference attributes are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:161
msgid ""
"`dir`: The subdirectory of the flake in which `flake.nix` is located. This "
"parameter enables having multiple flakes in a repository or tarball. The "
"default is the root directory of the flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:166
msgid ""
"`narHash`: The hash of the [Nix Archive (NAR) serialisation](../../store/"
"file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) (in [SRI](../../"
"glossary.md#gloss-sri) format) of the contents of the flake. This is useful "
"for flake types such as tarballs that lack a unique content identifier such "
"as a Git commit hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:173
msgid ""
"In addition, the following attributes are common to several flake reference "
"types:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:176
msgid "`rev`: A Git or Mercurial commit hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:178
msgid "`ref`: A Git or Mercurial branch or tag name."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:180
msgid ""
"Finally, some attributes are typically not specified by the user, but can "
"occur in _locked_ flake references and are available to Nix code:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:183
msgid "`revCount`: The number of ancestors of the commit `rev`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:185
msgid ""
"`lastModified`: The timestamp (in seconds since the Unix epoch) of the last "
"modification of this version of the flake. For Git/Mercurial flakes, this is "
"the commit time of commit _rev_, while for tarball flakes, it's the most "
"recent timestamp of any file inside the tarball."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:191
msgid "Types"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:193
msgid "Currently the `type` attribute can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:195
msgid ""
"`indirect`: _The default_. These are symbolic references to flakes that are "
"looked up in [the flake registries](./nix3-registry.md). These have the form"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:203
msgid ""
"These perform a lookup of `<flake-id>` in the flake registry. For example, "
"`nixpkgs` and `nixpkgs/release-20.09` are indirect flake references. The "
"specified `rev` and/or `ref` are merged with the entry in the registry; see "
"[nix registry](./nix3-registry.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:209
msgid "For example, these are valid indirect flake references:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:211
msgid "`nixpkgs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:212
msgid "`nixpkgs/nixos-unstable`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:213
msgid "`nixpkgs/a3a3dda3bacf61e8a39258a0ed9c924eeca8e293`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:214
msgid "`nixpkgs/nixos-unstable/a3a3dda3bacf61e8a39258a0ed9c924eeca8e293`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:215
msgid "`sub/dir` (if a flake named `sub` is in the registry)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:217
msgid ""
"<a id=\"path-fetcher\"></a>`path`: arbitrary local directories. The required "
"attribute `path` specifies the path of the flake. The URL form is"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:224
msgid ""
"where _path_ is an absolute path to a directory in the file system "
"containing a file named `flake.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:227
msgid ""
"If the flake at _path_ is not inside a git repository, the `path:` prefix is "
"implied and can be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:230
msgid ""
"If _path_ is a relative path (i.e. if it does not start with `/`), it is "
"interpreted as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:233
msgid ""
"If _path_ is a command line argument, it is interpreted relative to the "
"current directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:236
msgid ""
"If _path_ is used in a `flake.nix`, it is interpreted relative to the "
"directory containing that `flake.nix`. However, the resolved path must be in "
"the same tree. For instance, a `flake.nix` in the root of a tree can use "
"`path:./foo` to access the flake in subdirectory `foo`, but `path:../bar` is "
"illegal. On the other hand, a flake in the `/foo` directory of a tree can "
"use `path:../bar` to refer to the flake in `/bar`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:244
msgid ""
"Path inputs can be specified with path values in `flake.nix`. Path values "
"are a syntax for `path` inputs, and they are converted by"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:245
msgid ""
"resolving them into relative paths, relative to the base directory of "
"`flake.nix`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:246
msgid "escaping URL characters (refer to IETF RFC?)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:247
msgid "prepending `path:`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:249
msgid ""
"Note that the allowed syntax for path values in flake `inputs` may be more "
"restrictive than general Nix, so you may need to use `path:` if your path "
"contains certain special characters. See [Path literals](../../language/"
"syntax.md#path-literal)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:251
msgid ""
"Note that if you omit `path:`, relative paths must start with `.` to avoid "
"ambiguity with registry lookups (e.g. `nixpkgs` is a registry lookup; `./"
"nixpkgs` is a relative path)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:255
msgid "For example, these are valid path flake references:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:257
msgid "`path:/home/user/sub/dir`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:258
msgid "`/home/user/sub/dir` (if `dir/flake.nix` is _not_ in a git repository)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:259
msgid "`path:sub/dir`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:260
msgid "`./sub/dir`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:261
msgid "`path:../parent`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:263
msgid ""
"`git`: Git repositories. The location of the repository is specified by the "
"attribute `url`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:266
msgid "They have the URL form"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:268
msgid ""
"```\n"
"git(+http|+https|+ssh|+git|+file):(//<server>)?<path>(\\?<params>)?\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:272
msgid ""
"If _path_ starts with `/` (or `./` when used as an argument on the command "
"line) and is a local path to a git repository, the leading `git:` or `+file` "
"prefixes are implied and can be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:276
msgid "The `ref` attribute defaults to resolving the `HEAD` reference."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:278
msgid ""
"The `rev` attribute must denote a commit that exists in the branch or tag "
"specified by the `ref` attribute, since Nix doesn't do a full clone of the "
"remote repository by default (and the Git protocol doesn't allow fetching a "
"`rev` without a known `ref`). The default is the commit currently pointed to "
"by `ref`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:284
msgid ""
"When `git+file` is used without specifying `ref` or `rev`, files are fetched "
"directly from the local `path` as long as they have been added to the Git "
"repository. If there are uncommitted changes, the reference is treated as "
"dirty and a warning is printed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:289
msgid "For example, the following are valid Git flake references:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:291
msgid "`git:/home/user/sub/dir`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:292
msgid "`/home/user/sub/dir` (if `dir/flake.nix` is in a git repository)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:293
msgid ""
"`./sub/dir` (when used on the command line and `dir/flake.nix` is in a git "
"repository)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:294
msgid "`git+https://example.org/my/repo`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:295
msgid "`git+https://example.org/my/repo?dir=flake1`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:296
msgid ""
"`git+https://example.org/my/repo?shallow=1` A shallow clone of the "
"repository. For large repositories, the shallow clone option can "
"significantly speed up fresh clones compared to non-shallow clones, while "
"still providing faster updates than other fetch methods such as `tarball:` "
"or `github:`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:299
msgid "`git+ssh://git@github.com/NixOS/nix?ref=v1.2.3`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:300
msgid ""
"`git://github.com/edolstra/dwarffs?"
"ref=unstable&rev=e486d8d40e626a20e06d792db8cc5ac5aba9a5b4`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:301
msgid "`git+file:///home/my-user/some-repo/some-repo`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:303
msgid ""
"`mercurial`: Mercurial repositories. The URL form is similar to the `git` "
"type, except that the URL schema must be one of `hg+http`, `hg+https`, "
"`hg+ssh` or `hg+file`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:307
msgid ""
"`tarball`: Tarballs. The location of the tarball is specified by the "
"attribute `url`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:310
msgid ""
"In URL form, the schema must be `tarball+http://`, `tarball+https://` or "
"`tarball+file://`. If the extension corresponds to a known archive format "
"(`.zip`, `.tar`, `.tgz`, `.tar.gz`, `.tar.xz`, `.tar.bz2` or `.tar.zst`), "
"then the `tarball+` can be dropped."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:315
msgid ""
"This can also be used to set the location of gitea/forgejo branches. [See "
"here](../../protocols/tarball-fetcher.md#gitea-and-forgejo-support)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:317
msgid ""
"`file`: Plain files or directory tarballs, either over http(s) or from the "
"local disk."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:320
msgid ""
"In URL form, the schema must be `file+http://`, `file+https://` or "
"`file+file://`. If the extension doesn’t correspond to a known archive "
"format (as defined by the `tarball` fetcher), then the `file+` prefix can be "
"dropped."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:324
msgid ""
"`github`: A more efficient way to fetch repositories from GitHub. The "
"following attributes are required:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:327
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:360
msgid "`owner`: The owner of the repository."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:329
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:362
