#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:420
msgid "Flake format"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:422
msgid ""
"As an example, here is a simple `flake.nix` that depends on the Nixpkgs "
"flake and provides a single package (i.e. an [installable](./"
"nix.md#installables) derivation):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:426
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{\n"
"  description = \"A flake for building Hello World\";\n"
"\n"
"  inputs.nixpkgs.url = \"github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-20.03\";\n"
"\n"
"  outputs = { self, nixpkgs }: {\n"
"\n"
"    packages.x86_64-linux.default =\n"
"      # Notice the reference to nixpkgs here.\n"
"      with import nixpkgs { system = \"x86_64-linux\"; };\n"
"      stdenv.mkDerivation {\n"
"        name = \"hello\";\n"
"        src = self;\n"
"        buildPhase = \"gcc -o hello ./hello.c\";\n"
"        installPhase = \"mkdir -p $out/bin; install -t $out/bin hello\";\n"
"      };\n"
"\n"
"  };\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:448
msgid "The following attributes are supported in `flake.nix`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:450
msgid "`description`: A short, one-line description of the flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:452
msgid ""
"`inputs`: An attrset specifying the dependencies of the flake (described "
"below)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:455
msgid ""
"`outputs`: A function that, given an attribute set containing the outputs of "
"each of the input flakes keyed by their identifier, yields the Nix values "
"provided by this flake. Thus, in the example above, `inputs.nixpkgs` "
"contains the result of the call to the `outputs` function of the `nixpkgs` "
"flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:461
msgid ""
"In addition to the outputs of each input, each input in `inputs` also "
"contains some metadata about the inputs. These are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:464
msgid ""
"`outPath`: The path in the Nix store of the flake's source tree. This way, "
"the attribute set can be passed to `import` as if it was a path, as in the "
"example above (`import nixpkgs`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:468
msgid "`rev`: The commit hash of the flake's repository, if applicable."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:470
msgid ""
"`revCount`: The number of ancestors of the revision `rev`. This is not "
"available for `github` repositories, since they're fetched as tarballs "
"rather than as Git repositories."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:474
msgid ""
"`lastModifiedDate`: The commit time of the revision `rev`, in the format "
"`%Y%m%d%H%M%S` (e.g. `20181231100934`). Unlike `revCount`, this is available "
"for both Git and GitHub repositories, so it's useful for generating "
"(hopefully) monotonically increasing version strings."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:480
msgid ""
"`lastModified`: The commit time of the revision `rev` as an integer denoting "
"the number of seconds since 1970."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:483
msgid ""
"`narHash`: The SHA-256 (in [SRI](../../glossary.md#gloss-sri) format) of the "
"[Nix Archive (NAR) serialisation](../../store/file-system-object/content-"
"address.md#serial-nix-archive) NAR serialization of the flake's source tree."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:487
msgid ""
"The value returned by the `outputs` function must be an attribute set. The "
"attributes can have arbitrary values; however, various `nix` subcommands "
"require specific attributes to have a specific value (e.g. `packages.x86_64-"
"linux` must be an attribute set of derivations built for the `x86_64-linux` "
"platform)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:493
msgid ""
"`nixConfig`: a set of `nix.conf` options to be set when evaluating any part "
"of a flake. In the interests of security, only a small set of set of options "
"is allowed to be set without confirmation so long as [`accept-flake-config`]"
"(../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-accept-flake-config) is not enabled in "
"the global configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:496
msgid "[`bash-prompt`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-bash-prompt)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:497
msgid ""
"[`bash-prompt-prefix`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-bash-prompt-"
"prefix)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:498
msgid ""
"[`bash-prompt-suffix`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-bash-prompt-"
"suffix)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:499
msgid "[`flake-registry`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-flake-registry)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:500
msgid ""
"[`commit-lock-file-summary`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-commit-lock-"
"file-summary)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:502
msgid "Flake inputs"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:504
msgid ""
"The attribute `inputs` specifies the dependencies of a flake, as an attrset "
"mapping input names to flake references. For example, the following "
"specifies a dependency on the `nixpkgs` and `import-cargo` repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:509
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"# A GitHub repository.\n"
"inputs.import-cargo = {\n"
"  type = \"github\";\n"
"  owner = \"edolstra\";\n"
"  repo = \"import-cargo\";\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"# An indirection through the flake registry.\n"
"inputs.nixpkgs = {\n"
"  type = \"indirect\";\n"
"  id = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:524
msgid "Alternatively, you can use the URL-like syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:526
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.import-cargo.url = \"github:edolstra/import-cargo\";\n"
"inputs.nixpkgs.url = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:531
msgid ""
"Each input is fetched, evaluated and passed to the `outputs` function as a "
"set of attributes with the same name as the corresponding input. The special "
"input named `self` refers to the outputs and source tree of _this_ flake. "
"Thus, a typical `outputs` function looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:543
msgid ""
"It is also possible to omit an input entirely and _only_ list it as expected "
"function argument to `outputs`. Thus,"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:550
msgid "without an `inputs.nixpkgs` attribute is equivalent to"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:552
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.nixpkgs = {\n"
"  type = \"indirect\";\n"
"  id = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:559
msgid ""
"Repositories that don't contain a `flake.nix` can also be used as inputs, by "
"setting the input's `flake` attribute to `false`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:562
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.grcov = {\n"
"  type = \"github\";\n"
"  owner = \"mozilla\";\n"
"  repo = \"grcov\";\n"
"  flake = false;\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"outputs = { self, nixpkgs, grcov }: {\n"
"  packages.x86_64-linux.grcov = stdenv.mkDerivation {\n"
"    src = grcov;\n"
"    ...\n"
"  };\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:578
msgid ""
"Transitive inputs can be overridden from a `flake.nix` file. For example, "
"the following overrides the `nixpkgs` input of the `nixops` input:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:582
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.nixops.inputs.nixpkgs = {\n"
"  type = \"github\";\n"
"  owner = \"my-org\";\n"
"  repo = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:590
msgid ""
"It is also possible to \"inherit\" an input from another input. This is "
"useful to minimize flake dependencies. For example, the following sets the "
"`nixpkgs` input of the top-level flake to be equal to the `nixpkgs` input of "
"the `dwarffs` input of the top-level flake:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:595
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.nixpkgs.follows = \"dwarffs/nixpkgs\";\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:599
msgid ""
"The value of the `follows` attribute is a `/`\\-separated sequence of input "
"names denoting the path of inputs to be followed from the root flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:603
msgid "Self-attributes"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:605
msgid ""
"Flakes can declare attributes about themselves that affect how they are "
"fetched. These attributes are specified using the special `self` input and "
"are retroactively applied to it:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:616
msgid "The following self-attributes are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:618
msgid ""
"`submodules`: A Boolean denoting whether Git submodules should be fetched "
"when this flake is used as an input. When set to `true`, Git submodules will "
"be automatically fetched without requiring callers to specify `submodules=1` "
"in the flake reference URL. Defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:620
msgid ""
"`lfs`: A Boolean denoting whether Git LFS (Large File Storage) files should "
"be fetched when this flake is used as an input. When set to `true`, Git LFS "
"files will be automatically fetched. Defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:622
msgid ""
"These self-attributes eliminate the need for consumers of your flake to "
"manually specify fetching options in their flake references."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:624
msgid "Overrides and `follows` can be combined, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:626
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.nixops.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = \"dwarffs/nixpkgs\";\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:630
msgid ""
"sets the `nixpkgs` input of `nixops` to be the same as the `nixpkgs` input "
"of `dwarffs`. It is worth noting, however, that it is generally not useful "
"to eliminate transitive `nixpkgs` flake inputs in this way. Most flakes "
"provide their functionality through Nixpkgs overlays or NixOS modules, which "
"are composed into the top-level flake's `nixpkgs` input; so their own "
"`nixpkgs` input is usually irrelevant."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:637
msgid "Lock files"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:639
msgid ""
"Inputs specified in `flake.nix` are typically \"unlocked\" in the sense that "
"they don't specify an exact revision. To ensure reproducibility, Nix will "
"automatically generate and use a _lock file_ called `flake.lock` in the "
"flake's directory. The lock file is a UTF-8 JSON file. It contains a graph "
"structure isomorphic to the graph of dependencies of the root flake. Each "
"node in the graph (except the root node) maps the (usually) unlocked input "
"specifications in `flake.nix` to locked input specifications. Each node also "
"contains some metadata, such as the dependencies (outgoing edges) of the "
"node."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:650
msgid ""
"For example, if `flake.nix` has the inputs in the example above, then the "
"resulting lock file might be:"
msgstr ""

